From 3cd105a72eab44a167bead355de31e91e00053a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:12:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(helper): list-cameras, the cameras libcamera finds by id

Platform cameras behind one CSI-2 receiver (e.g. Qualcomm CAMSS on
Snapdragon laptops) share all their /dev/video nodes, so the app's
device list cannot tell an IR sensor from the colour sensor next to it:
only libcamera's camera id names one (config.yaml's `camera` and
`anti_spoofing.ir_camera` already take it, see findCameraByPath).

`biopass-helper list-cameras` prints one line per camera: id, `mono` or
`colour` (a sensor without colour filters, as libcamera reports it: an
IR camera), its video nodes and its model, tab-separated
(face/common/camera_list.h). CameraDeviceInfo carries the mono flag.
Test: camera_list.
